{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`rebar-root-disk-pressure` (account 896586841071, us-east-1) went OK→ALARM 2026-08-17 21:51:56\nPDT and back 22:12:56 on `rebar-gerrit` (`i-00880b2c7f13527c5`, 30-GiB gp3 root). Root usage\nclimbed 71% @20:55 → 90% @21:55/22:00, then dropped to 48% @22:05. `reviewbot_healthy` dipped\nto 0 at 22:05; `deploy_deferrals` 2/3/1 at 21:55/22:00/22:05; zero `voter_errors` and\n`deploy_errors`.\n\n## Phase 1: COMPLETE — root cause proven\n\nFull evidence in the \"Phase 1 EXIT\" comment (experiments, CloudWatch series, citations).\nSummary:\n\n- **REJECTED — \"autodeploy prunes Docker caches too late.\"** Build artifacts cannot appear\n  without a build; 10 of 12 build-free intervals still grew (median +1.12, max +3.93 GiB/h).\n  The 12.6-GiB reclaim exceeds the whole 5 GB buildkit ceiling. `prune_docker_caches` cannot\n  reclaim a **running** container's writable layer at all.\n- **CONFIRMED (RC-B, this ticket) — the janitor's reclaim triggers are unreachable here.**\n  `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:53` `DEFAULT_FREE_WATERMARK_BYTES = 2 GiB` is an **absolute**,\n  disk-size-blind floor: on a 30-GiB root it is crossed only at **93.3% used**, above the 85%\n  alarm (`infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:226`) and above the 90% peak reached.\n  Driving the real `run_gc()` with injected free space gives **0 evictions at 85% and at 90%\n  used**; first eviction only past 93.3%. The 7-day cold-trim (`janitor.py:55`) exceeds the\n  container's lifetime (23 recreations in 4 days). The janitor *is* started\n  (`src/rebar/review_bot/app.py:134-136`) and correctly evicted nothing.\n- **CONFIRMED (RC-A, split to `smart-disloyal-naga`) — the growth source.** Every review\n  materializes a full ~620 MiB / 69,984-file copy of the ticket tree\n  (`src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py:99` → `_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:675-703`), keyed on a tip\n  that advanced 1,374 times in the 10-hour window with consecutive commits differing by 1 file.\n\nThe store sits on the 30-GiB root because `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` is unset everywhere, so\n`store_root()` (`repo_snapshot.py:113`) falls through to `tempfile.gettempdir()` = the\ncontainer writable layer. The 48% floor and the 22:05 health dip are one event:\n`docker compose up -d review-bot` recreating the container and destroying that layer.\n\n## Scope of THIS ticket\n\nRC-B only — make reclaim engage **before** the operator's alarm floor. RC-A is\n`smart-disloyal-naga`; the missing byte-total backstop and the missing `add_bytes` accounting\nfor `tickets-<sha>` entries are `itchy-arbored-peccary`.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd a **volume-relative** headroom term to the janitor's free-space trigger so the watermark\ncannot sit above the alarm floor on a small volume, plus hysteresis so a pass reclaims past the\ntrigger instead of re-firing every 300 s. Both new values are **integers** so they survive the\nexisting int-only config seam (`_snapshot_int` coerces with `int()`, and `JanitorConfig`'s\nfields and `_default_tunables()` are `dict[str, int]`) — a float fraction would truncate to 0\nand silently disable the fix.\n\n1. `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py` — add `DEFAULT_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT = 0` and\n   `free_watermark_pct: int` (whole percent of the volume; `0` = relative term off) to\n   `JanitorConfig` + `_default_tunables()`. Add a module-level\n   `RECLAIM_TARGET_MARGIN_PCT = 5` constant — a fixed internal margin, not an operator knob,\n   matching how `DEFAULT_GRACE_SECONDS` / `DEFAULT_INTERVAL_SECONDS` are handled. In\n   `_gc_pass`, take `total = shutil.disk_usage(root).total` and compute:\n   - `trigger = max(free_watermark_bytes, total * free_watermark_pct // 100)`\n   - `target  = max(free_watermark_bytes, total * (free_watermark_pct + RECLAIM_TARGET_MARGIN_PCT) // 100)`\n\n   Evict when `free < trigger`, and once triggered keep evicting until `free >= target`. The\n   grace window and `_is_entry`'s `tickets-` recognition are untouched.\n\n   Worked example, 30-GiB root, `free_watermark_pct = 20`: `trigger` = 6.0 GiB free (80% used),\n   `target` = 7.5 GiB free (75% used). Both sit below the 85% alarm floor (4.5 GiB free), which\n   is what AC4 requires. With `free_watermark_pct = 0` the arithmetic collapses to\n   `max(2 GiB, 0)` = today's behaviour exactly.\n\n2. `src/rebar/_config_sources.py` — resolve `free_watermark_pct` through the existing\n   `resolve_janitor_tunables` int path (`REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT` > `[snapshot]` table >\n   default `0`). No new float helper is needed.\n3. `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` — set `REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT: \"20\"` on the\n   `review-bot` service, the pattern already used for `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` and\n   `REBAR_USAGE_LOG`. 20 is `autodeploy.sh:110`'s `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT=80` expressed as headroom,\n   chosen there as below the 85% alarm for hysteresis.\n4. `docs/config.md`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`, `docs/env-vars.md` — document the one new\n   knob and the fixed margin.\n5. `tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py` — the RED oracle.\n\n### Design decision for review: what should `free_watermark_pct` default to?\n\n- **Option A (this plan) — default `0` (off), set to `20` for the review-bot host in compose.**\n  No behaviour change for any existing rebar user; fixes this host. Cost: the defect stays\n  latent for other deployments on small volumes.\n- **Option B — default `20`.** Removes the defect for every deployment. Cost: on a large volume\n  that is >80% full for unrelated reasons, `_gc_pass` would evict the whole store every pass\n  without reaching the target. Bounding how much such a pass evicts needs the store's real\n  size — exactly the accounting `itchy-arbored-peccary` restores, so Option B should follow it.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun from the worktree venv (`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" ...`).\n\n- **RED oracle** — `pytest tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py -q`. New cases drive the real\n  `janitor.run_gc()` with `free_bytes` injected for a 30-GiB volume (`total` stubbed via\n  `shutil.disk_usage`): at 85% used (4.50 GiB free) and at 90% used (3.00 GiB free) the pass\n  MUST evict a non-grace entry. Against current code both evict 0 — the observed RED. A\n  hysteresis case asserts the pass continues to the 7.5-GiB-free target rather than stopping\n  at the 6.0-GiB trigger; a grace case asserts an entry touched inside `grace_seconds` is still\n  skipped. A `free_watermark_pct=0` case asserts today's behaviour is unchanged.\n- **Exact-defect mutation** — reset the compose/config `free_watermark_pct` to 0 (restoring\n  the absolute-only watermark) and re-run the module: the new cases MUST return to RED.\n- **Config seam** — `pytest tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py -k tunable -q`, covering\n  `REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT=20` surviving int resolution (not truncating to 0).\n- **Docs pin** — `pytest tests/unit/test_snapshot_docs.py -q`.\n- **No regression** — `pytest tests/unit -q`; `make lint`; `make typecheck`; `make config-check`.\n- **Post-deploy (operator, read-only)** — `rebar/host:root_disk_used_percent` shows reclaim\n  events with peaks under 85%, where the pre-fix series peaked at 90% (2026-08-17) and 87%\n  (2026-08-18).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A faithful local reproduction identifies the dominant disk consumer and the component\n      responsible for the 90%→48% reclaim.\n- [x] A discriminating runtime experiment proves the root cause and rules out the surviving\n      Docker-vs-snapshot alternative.\n- [ ] A test is observed RED on the proven mechanism, GREEN after repair, then RED again under\n      the exact-defect mutation — proved by `pytest tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py -q`.\n- [ ] The repaired path reclaims before a 30-GiB root crosses the 85% alarm floor — proved by\n      the 4.50-GiB-free case evicting.\n- [ ] The repaired path reclaims with hysteresis — proved by the hysteresis case asserting\n      reclaim continues to the 7.5-GiB-free target, not stopping at the 6.0-GiB trigger.\n- [ ] Live/grace snapshot entries are preserved — proved by the grace-window case.\n- [ ] Existing fail-safe deploy/review semantics remain intact — proved by `pytest tests/unit -q`\n      green (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` is absent from this ticket's file impact).\n- [ ] Documentation is updated — proved by `pytest tests/unit/test_snapshot_docs.py -q` green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787174542813273001,"uuid":"335088eb-764a-48e7-97f5-573d8420cd22"}